lStorage for admin content management.\"\n\nSo it's a separate auth system. I should create an admin_sessions table and make admin_login.php create proper sessions.\n\nActually, the simplest and most compatible fix is:\n1. Create an `admin_sessions` table in the migration\n2. Store sessions in admin_login.php when created\n3. Add a verify endpoint for admin sessions\n4. Add a logout endpoint that destroys admin sessions\n\nLet me implement this.\n\n### Fix 2: checkRateLimit - Fix function signature\nThe function needs to accept custom limits.\n\n### Fix 3: getAuthUser - Add patient_sessions support\nModify the query to also check patient_sessions.\n\n### Fix 4: cleanupExpiredSessions - Add patient sessions cleanup\n\n### Fix 5: destroySession - Handle patient sessions\n\n### Fix 6: sendSecurityHeaders - Call it\n\n### Fix 7: Remove duplicate CSRF functions\n\n### Fix 8: Password complexity validation\n\n### Fix 9: Account lockout\n\n### Fix 10: Email verification\n\n### Fix 11: Password reset endpoint\n\n### Fix 12: Fix setup.php\n\nLet me start implementing. I'll work through each fix methodically.\n\nLet me think about the order and do it efficiently.\n\nFirst, let me check what other API files exist to understand the full picture."
